From 2a074fb85d78d065df5c529d7c0d748454bcaa3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiebing Li <jiebing.li@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Dec 2014 05:26:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: gadget: release spin lock during gadget resume

Reference-only copy of the upstream source change applied by A2L5E0X1
on 2026-11-08 to exynos7885-dev's Linux 4.4.302 kernel. This is NOT
a Linux 5.10/5.15 forward-port or a flashable Android 17 change.
Upstream commit: 2a074fb85d78d065df5c529d7c0d748454bcaa3a
Upstream parent: 6020dfa8315134187f07ca903c9d2ed7ee0256f5

It's a requirement that we release controller's lock
while calling gadget API function pointers. This
patch just fixes that long standing bug.

Change-Id: Id4ccbaca290c0088933a2bc951e42947573fbfb8
Signed-off-by: Jiebing Li <jiebing.li@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Felipe Balbi <felipe.balbi@linux.intel.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
@@ -2993,7 +2993,9 @@ static void dwc3_gadget_wakeup_interrupt(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 	 */
 
 	if (dwc->gadget_driver && dwc->gadget_driver->resume) {
+		spin_unlock(&dwc->lock);
 		dwc->gadget_driver->resume(&dwc->gadget);
+		spin_lock(&dwc->lock);
 	}
 }
 
